"G-Shock has Timekeeping, Alarm, Countdown and Stopwatch modes. A adjusts settings, records a split or resets; B starts/stops or increments; C changes mode or field; D illuminates the LCD. Hold B for two seconds in Timekeeping to toggle Flash Alert. Interaction offers the same controls and alarm/timer settings without the case.\n\nThe stopwatch supports split times and two finishes. The countdown runs from 1 second to 24 hours with optional auto-repeat. The alarm can be daily or limited by month/day; an hourly signal is also available. Stopwatch and countdown states are saved and restored after relaunch. Running timers include time while the app is closed. An overdue countdown sounds once on the next launch; auto-repeat preserves the cycle phase. Manual pause and reset remain in effect. Time follows macOS; A in Timekeeping selects only the 12/24-hour format, changed with D.\n\nSound requires the app to remain running. The app does not wake a sleeping Mac; overdue alarms are checked after wake, including when another theme is selected." = "G-Shock has Timekeeping, Alarm, Countdown and Stopwatch modes. A adjusts settings, records a split or resets; B starts/stops or increments; C changes mode or field; D illuminates the LCD. Hold B for two seconds in Timekeeping to toggle Flash Alert. Interaction offers the same controls and alarm/timer settings without the case.\n\nThe stopwatch supports split times and two finishes. The countdown runs from 1 second to 24 hours with optional auto-repeat. The alarm can be daily or limited by month/day; an hourly signal is also available. Stopwatch and countdown states are saved and restored after relaunch. Running timers include time while the app is closed. An overdue countdown sounds once on the next launch; auto-repeat preserves the cycle phase. Manual pause and reset remain in effect. Time follows macOS; A in Timekeeping selects only the 12/24-hour format, changed with D.\n\nSound requires the app to remain running. The app does not wake a sleeping Mac; overdue alarms are checked after wake, including when another theme is selected.";

